      "full_text": "More (AIM is for Aboriginal and Islander Mob) was an Indigenous Australian band. They released their debut self-titled CD in 1997. They won a Deadly in 1997 for Most Promising New Talent. They were features in the ABC TV show Defining Black. Discography AIM 4 More (1997) - JamalgaAim 4 More (AIM is for Aboriginal and Islander Mob) was an Indigenous Australian band that made significant contributions to the music scene, blending contemporary sounds with traditional influences. They released their debut self-titled CD in 1997, which included tracks like \"Jamalga\" among others. The album showcased a mix of genres including hip-hop, rock, and soul. Discography: - Aim 4 More (1997): This debut album not only earned them critical acclaim but also a Deadly Award in the same year for Most Promising New Talent. Tracks like \"Jamalga\" highlighted their unique sound and cultural storytelling. The band's participation in the ABc TV show further cemented their place in Australian music history, providing a platform to share their stories and musical talents with a broader audience.",
